        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It’s the summer of 1986 in Lakeshore: neon nights, mixtapes, and the warm glow of Sunset Video—a mom-and-pop rental store hanging by a thread as the slick Video King chain moves in. You’re a 20-year-old, player-named MC with a secret (you dropped out) and a dream you barely admit to yourself (becoming a filmmaker). Over one unforgettable week, you’ll rally the town, save or lose the store, and fall in love.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Six fully branched romance routes</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Choose your path with <strong>Veronica</strong> (warm store owner), <strong>Helen</strong> (guarded goth), <strong>Lucy</strong> (sunny mascot), <strong>Chloe</strong> (shy coder), <strong>Tessa</strong> (tomboy best friend) or <strong>Sloane</strong> (aloof salon owner). Each woman has her own inner conflict, chemistry, and Act III story where you film a short starring her from neon music-video vibes to moody horror and skate docu-drama.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Your choices matter (no stat-grind, no minigames)</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a pure visual novel: branching dialogue choices only. Mid-game, your decisions lock a route (or lead to a solo “director” path). Your community actions also decide whether Sunset Video is saved or shuttered, a turning point that changes what follows.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >14 endings, built for replay</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>12 heroine endings</strong> (2 per route)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1 philosophical solo ending</strong> (no romance, creative fulfillment)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1 early bad ending</strong> if the store closes</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >SFW and comfortable by design</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >100% SFW. Expect yearning looks, kisses, and tasteful fade-to-black.  All characters are clearly 18+, all romance is clearly consensual, no explicit content.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It’s the summer of 1986 in Lakeshore: neon nights, mixtapes, and the warm glow of Sunset Video—a mom-and-pop rental store hanging by a thread as the slick Video King chain moves in. You’re a 20-year-old, player-named MC with a secret (you dropped out) and a dream you barely admit to yourself (becoming a filmmaker). Over one unforgettable week, you’ll rally the town, save or lose the store, and fall in love.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Six fully branched romance routes</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Choose your path with <strong>Veronica</strong> (warm store owner), <strong>Helen</strong> (guarded goth), <strong>Lucy</strong> (sunny mascot), <strong>Chloe</strong> (shy coder), <strong>Tessa</strong> (tomboy best friend) or <strong>Sloane</strong> (aloof salon owner). Each woman has her own inner conflict, chemistry, and Act III story where you film a short starring her from neon music-video vibes to moody horror and skate docu-drama.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Your choices matter (no stat-grind, no minigames)</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a pure visual novel: branching dialogue choices only. Mid-game, your decisions lock a route (or lead to a solo “director” path). Your community actions also decide whether Sunset Video is saved or shuttered, a turning point that changes what follows.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >14 endings, built for replay</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>12 heroine endings</strong> (2 per route)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1 philosophical solo ending</strong> (no romance, creative fulfillment)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1 early bad ending</strong> if the store closes</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >SFW and comfortable by design</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >100% SFW. Expect yearning looks, kisses, and tasteful fade-to-black.  All characters are clearly 18+, all romance is clearly consensual, no explicit content.</p>",
